# How git should treat the bytes in this repository.
#
# Three jobs: keep line endings from becoming a diff, keep vendored and
# generated files out of review and out of GitHub's language stats, and give
# git the hunk-header rules that make a diff readable.
#
# NOT here on purpose: `export-ignore`. It would trim files out of the tarball
# GitHub generates for a tag, and that tarball is exactly what `zig fetch`
# hashes - the url+hash pin a downstream `build.zig.zon` carries is a hash of
# those bytes. Excluding a directory to save a consumer a few kilobytes would
# invalidate every pin that already exists. What ships in the Zig package is
# already decided, deliberately and reviewably, by `.paths` in build.zig.zon.

# ── Line endings ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Normalize on commit, LF in the working tree on every platform. Everything
# here is built by Zig, Go, Rust, Python, and POSIX shell; none of them wants
# CRLF, and a Windows checkout that introduced it would fail the corpus tests
# by changing the bytes under test.
* text=auto eol=lf

# ── Binary ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The prebuilt per-platform archives the Go and Rust bindings link, so that a
# consumer needs no Zig toolchain. Explicitly binary: they are large, and a
# heuristic that ever guessed "text" would try to normalize them.
*.a binary

# ── Vendored ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Upstream sources we carry verbatim - PCRE2 behind `-P`, libsais under the
# FM-index, and the Rust binding's vendored archives. `linguist-vendored`
# keeps them out of the repository's language breakdown; the C in PCRE2 is
# not this project's C.
vendor/**                 linguist-vendored
bindings/rust/vendor/**   linguist-vendored

# The pinned Unicode Character Database and WHATWG encoding tables. Inputs to
# the table generators under tools/, not source anyone edits by hand.
tools/ucd/**     linguist-vendored -diff
tools/whatwg/**  linguist-vendored -diff

# ── Generated ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The schema tables every face lowers through, minted by
# tools/build_schema_tables.py from contract/*.toml. Collapsed in review
# because the diff to read is the contract's, not its projection's.
*.gen.zig      linguist-generated
schema.gen.*   linguist-generated
schema_gen.*   linguist-generated

# The C header and archives the bindings carry are copies placed by their
# `scripts/vendor_libraries.py`; the source of truth is include/irgx.h and
# `zig build`.
bindings/*/irgx.h  linguist-generated

# Lockfiles: resolver output. Reviewed as a fact ("this version moved"), never
# read line by line.
*.lock  linguist-generated -diff

# ── Diff drivers ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Git ships hunk-header patterns for these languages; naming them here is what
# makes `@@ ... fn whatever` appear above a hunk instead of a bare line number.
*.c   diff=cpp
*.h   diff=cpp
*.go  diff=golang
*.py  diff=python
*.rs  diff=rust
*.md  diff=markdown

# Zig has no built-in driver. The attribute is inert until the pattern exists
# in your own git config; CONTRIBUTING.md has the one-line command, and
# without it this line simply falls back to git's default behaviour.
*.zig diff=zig

# ── Merge ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The changelog is append-at-the-top and assembled by towncrier. Two branches
# adding release sections conflict textually while agreeing semantically; a
# union merge keeps both and lets the next `towncrier build` sort it out.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
